<h1>Croatian Subcategorization  Grammar for Natural Language Generation</h1>Version of September 11, 2026, 1:02 pm<br />Documentation available at <a href="http://www.unlarchive.org/wiki/index.php/Grammar" target="_blank">http://www.unlarchive.org/wiki/index.php/Grammar</a><br />Tagset available at <a href="../dictionary/export_tagset.php" target="_blank">Export UNDL Foundation tagset</a>.<br /><br /><b>Y0</b><br />AVALENT<br /><br /><b>Y1</b><br />NO SUBCATEGORIZATION FRAME: rules defined inside the entry in the dictionary<br /><br /><b>Y102</b><br />Verbs that do not take any objects. (<i>spavati, umrijeti, večerati, trčati</i>)<br />VS(NP);<br /><br /><b>Y103</b><br />Transitive verbs that require a direct object in accusative. (<i>peći, kupiti, saznati, čitati</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP,ACC);<br /><br /><b>Y104</b><br />Verbs whose reflexive pronoun "se" can be replaced by its longer form "sebe". (<i>odijevati se, češljati se, umivati se, presvlačiti se, uprljati se</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(FPR);<br /><br /><b>Y105</b><br />Indirect transitive verbs that require an object in genitive. (<i>bojati se, plašiti se, sramiti se, libiti se, groziti se, užasavati se, sjetiti se, uhvatiti se, dočepati se, riješiti se;</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP,GEN);<br /><br /><b>Y106</b><br />Transitive verbs that require an indirect object in locative, which is preceded by the preposition "u". (<i>uživati, napredovati, ustrajati</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(PC([u];NP,LOC));<br /><br /><b>Y107</b><br />Transitive verbs that require an object in instrumental, which is preceded by the preposition "za". (<i>patiti, žudjeti, trčati, plakati, tragati</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(PC([za];NP,INS));<br /><br /><b>Y108</b><br />Transitive verbs that require an object in accusative, which is preceded by the preposition "na". (<i>utjecati, ciljati, pripaziti, naletjeti, baciti pogled, osloniti se</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(PC([na];NP,ACC));<br /><br /><b>Y109</b><br />Transitive verbs that require an object in dative. (<i>vjerovati, prijetiti, pomagati, služiti</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP,DAT);<br /><br /><b>Y110</b><br />Transitive verbs that require an indirect object in locative, which is preceded by the preposition "o". (<i>ovisiti, govoriti, razmišljati, maštati</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(PC([o];NP,LOC));<br /><br /><b>Y111</b><br />Transitive verbs that require an indirect object in dative, which is preceded by the preposition "na". (<i>zahvaliti, inzistirati</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(PC([na];NP,DAT));<br /><br /><b>Y112</b><br />Transitive verbs that require an object in accusative, which is preceded by the preposition "u". (<i>vjerovati, pretvoriti se</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(PC([u];NP,ACC));<br /><br /><b>Y113</b><br />Transitive verbs that require an indirect object in instrumental, which is preceded by the preposition "s". (<i>razgovarati, svađati se</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(PC([s];NP,INS));<br /><br /><b>Y114</b><br />Transitive verbs that require an object in accusative, which is preceded by the preposition "za". (<i>brinuti se, zalagati se, strepjeti</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(PC([za];NP,ACC));<br /><br /><b>Y115</b><br />Transitive verbs that require an object in instrumental. (<i>poslužiti se, ponositi se, zasladiti se</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP,INS);<br /><br /><b>Y116</b><br />Verbs that require two objects, one in accusative and the other in genitive. The object in genitive is preceded by the preposition "od". (<i>braniti, štititi</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP,ACC)VC(PH([od]));<br /><br /><b>Y117</b><br />Verbs that require two objects, one in accusative and the other in locative. The object in locative is preceded by the preposition "o". (<i>obavijestiti, informirati</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP,ACC)VC(PC([o];NP,LOC));<br /><br /><b>Y118</b><br />Verbs that require two objects in accusative. The second object is preceded by the preposition "na". (<i>upozoriti, podsjetiti</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP,ACC)VC(PC([na];NP,ACC));<br /><br /><b>Y119</b><br />Verbs that require one direct object in accusative and one indirect object in dative. (<i>dati, reći, učiniti</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP,ACC)VC(NP,DAT);<br /><br /><b>Y120</b><br />Verbs that require two objects, one in dative and the other in accusative. The object in accusative is precede by the preposition "na". (<i>ukazati</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP,DAT)VC(PC([na];NP,ACC));<br /><br /><b>Y121</b><br />Verbs that require two objects, one in accusative and the other in instrumental. (<i>povrijediti, učiniti, posluživati</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP,ACC)VC(NP,INS);<br /><br /><b>Y122</b><br />Verbs that require two objects, both in accusative. The second object is preceded by the preposition "za". (<i>kriviti, zamoliti</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP,ACC)VC(PC([za];NP,ACC));<br /><br /><b>Y123</b><br />Verbs that require two objects, one in accusative and the other in locative. The object in locative is preceded by the preposition "u". (<i>pobijediti</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP,ACC)VC(PC([u];NP,LOC));<br /><br /><b>Y124</b><br />Verbs that require an object in dative. (<i>veseliti se, radovati se, sličiti, prisustvovati, smetati, smijati se, diviti se, čuditi se, približavati se, zahvaljivati, nadati se</i>)<br />VS(NP)VC(NP,DAT);<br /><br /><b>Y125</b><br />Adjectives requiring complement introduced by "za". (<i>odgovoran, predodređen, sposoban, nesposoban</i>)<br />JC(PH([za]));<br /><br /><b>Y126</b><br />Adjectives requiring complement introduced by "o". (<i>ovisan</i>)<br />JC(PH([o]));<br /><br /><b>Y127</b><br />Adjectives requiring complement introduced by "na". (<i>imun, osuđen, prisiljen</i>)<br />JC(PH([na]));<br /><br /></body>
